row    B0B60Y12 1900 [44] ___dungeon_ are yours for your trouble, %pcf
row    B0B60Y12 1900 [41] - the old woman has no more use for them.
row    B0B60Y12 1900 [19] Will you take them?
label  B0B60Y12 1901 [25] I accept the heir's gift.
label  B0B60Y12 1902 [26] Leave them with her ashes.
row    B0B70Y14 1900 [43] _qgiver_ holds out a purse of gold - an odd
row    B0B70Y14 1900 [40] thing, in an order that does not pay its
row    B0B70Y14 1900 [22] own. Will you take it?
label  B0B70Y14 1901 [21] I will take the gold.
label  B0B70Y14 1902 [22] No. I fight for glory.
row    B0B70Y14 1903 [42] So you killed the Daedra, eh? It turns out
row    B0B70Y14 1903 [43] we were duped by a rogue mage. She summoned
row    B0B70Y14 1903 [43] a Daedra she could not control, and told us
row    B0B70Y14 1903 [38] her story so we would slay it for free
row    B0B70Y14 1903 [44] rather than pay the Fighters Guild. You will
row    B0B70Y14 1903 [42] not take her gold? Then the Fighters Guild
row    B0B70Y14 1903 [41] shall have it - it is the fee she cheated
row    B0B70Y14 1903 [8] them of.
row    B0B70Y16 1900 [39] The order will ask who slew the dragon,
row    B0B70Y16 1900 [41] %pcf. As we agreed - we both stood before
row    B0B70Y16 1900 [37] it. You will tell them so, won't you?
label  B0B70Y16 1901 [23] A bargain is a bargain.
label  B0B70Y16 1902 [30] I'll tell the order the truth.
row    B0B70Y16 1903 [44] You tell the order the truth of the dragon's
row    B0B70Y16 1903 [43] death. All hail %pcn, known from this point
row    B0B70Y16 1903 [43] onward as a dragonslayer! _qgiver_ will not
row    B0B70Y16 1903 [15] meet your eyes.
row    B0B80Y17 1900 [43] The lich's books of necromancy still lie in
row    B0B80Y17 1900 [40] its lair in ___dungeon_, %pcf. The Mages
row    B0B80Y17 1900 [41] Guild offers good coin to study them; the
row    B0B80Y17 1900 [43] temple would see them burned. The choice is
row    B0B80Y17 1900 [21] yours - you won them.
