row    B0B50Y11 1903 [42] folk, and no name upon it. _nobleman_ will
row    B0B50Y11 1903 [24] be pleased all the same.
row    N0B40Y07 1900 [37] Banished, and none the worse for it -
row    N0B40Y07 1900 [36] exactly as I wanted. Now, my scroll,
row    N0B40Y07 1900 [33] if you please. That is =daedra_'s
row    N0B40Y07 1900 [33] true name you are carrying, and I
row    N0B40Y07 1900 [28] shall have need of it again.
label  N0B40Y07 1901 [20] Here is your scroll.
label  N0B40Y07 1902 [23] I will burn the scroll.
row    L0A01L00 1900 [44] Before the custom is kept, %pcn: a novice is
row    L0A01L00 1900 [37] paid a single gold coin for the first
row    L0A01L00 1900 [43] sanctioned death - and the devout give that
row    L0A01L00 1900 [34] coin to Mephala. Which will it be?
label  L0A01L00 1901 [14] Take the coin.
label  L0A01L00 1902 [19] Give it to Mephala.
row    L0A01L00 1903 [40] Well done, %pcn. _npc_ was stricken with
row    L0A01L00 1903 [44] sudden heart failure. You have shown you can
row    L0A01L00 1903 [40] kill with care and not just with a bared
row    L0A01L00 1903 [44] blade. You are now a full member of the Dark
row    L0A01L00 1903 [42] Brotherhood. Anytime you enter a town, you
row    L0A01L00 1903 [42] will know if there are any guild buildings
row    L0A01L00 1903 [33] there. Your coin goes to Mephala.
row    L0B40Y04 1900 [41] _knight_ will not see the throne, and our
row    L0B40Y04 1900 [43] client sits a step nearer to it. A royal so
row    L0B40Y04 1900 [40] near a crown is worth more to us in debt
row    L0B40Y04 1900 [44] than in coin, %pcf. Your fee - will you take
row    L0B40Y04 1900 [40] it, or let it stand as a debt the client
row    L0B40Y04 1900 [21] owes the Brotherhood?
label  L0B40Y04 1901 [24] The gold, as contracted.
label  L0B40Y04 1902 [19] Let the debt stand.
row    L0B60Y10 1900 [42] Before I pay you, %pcf: the old accounters
row    L0B60Y10 1900 [41] would spend a fee like this on the mark's
row    L0B60Y10 1900 [41] rites. Nine men killed in the Betony war,
row    L0B60Y10 1900 [39] the stories say. That deserves a better
row    L0B60Y10 1900 [31] grave than gossip. Your choice.
label  L0B60Y10 1901 [13] Take the fee.
label  L0B60Y10 1902 [28] Pay for the veteran's rites.
