row    A0C01Y03 1903 [42] "Kindness! Of course. Now I understand why
row    A0C01Y03 1903 [41] _spouse_ sent me on this quest. It is not
row    A0C01Y03 1903 [38] enough to love %g2, I have to show %g2
row    A0C01Y03 1903 [44] kindness as well. And you have shown me how,
row    A0C01Y03 1903 [6] %pcf."
row    A0C01Y06 1900 [42] Look - finish off _master_, and the gold I
row    A0C01Y06 1900 [42] was paid to send you there is yours. Every
row    A0C01Y06 1900 [44] coin. Only keep my name away from the guard,
row    A0C01Y06 1900 [3] eh?
label  A0C01Y06 1901 [27] Take the gold. Say nothing.
label  A0C01Y06 1902 [30] No. The guard will hear of it.
row    A0C01Y06 1903 [41] _qgiver_ goes pale. "You wouldn't..." But
row    A0C01Y06 1903 [40] you would, and the guard will hear of it
row    A0C01Y06 1903 [22] before the day is out.
row    A0C01Y13 1900 [43] Home, at last! I owe you my life, %pcn. Now
row    A0C01Y13 1900 [41] give me that letter. _giver_ and _sister_
row    A0C01Y13 1900 [35] will learn what it is to be afraid.
label  A0C01Y13 1901 [24] Give _lover_ the letter.
label  A0C01Y13 1902 [27] Keep it for the magistrate.
row    A0C01Y13 1903 [44] _lover_ stares at you, then laughs bitterly.
row    A0C01Y13 1903 [42] "The magistrate, then. Much good may it do
row    A0C01Y13 1903 [44] you. You have my thanks - and nothing more."
row    A0C41Y18 1900 [42] Of course, there is the coward's way - the
row    A0C41Y18 1900 [39] way of whoever gave it to you. Give the
row    A0C41Y18 1900 [41] _finger_ to some other poor soul, and the
row    A0C41Y18 1900 [44] mummy will follow it instead of you. I would
row    A0C41Y18 1900 [29] not. But the choice is yours.
label  A0C41Y18 1901 [18] Destroy the mummy.
label  A0C41Y18 1902 [21] Pass the _finger_ on.
row    A0C41Y18 1903 [40] The next stranger on the road takes your
row    A0C41Y18 1903 [43] package without a second look. Tonight, the
row    A0C41Y18 1903 [33] mummy will come for someone else.
row    Q0C4XY04 1900 [39] Thou hast it, %pcn, and still it beats!
row    Q0C4XY04 1900 [43] Quickly now, before it cools - what wouldst
row    Q0C4XY04 1900 [41] thou have of thy poor aunts for so fine a
row    Q0C4XY04 1900 [6] heart?
label  Q0C4XY04 1901 [26] The _reward_ you promised.
label  Q0C4XY04 1902 [29] Nothing. A gift for my aunts.
row    P0A01L00 1900 [44] The lesser one is ash, and %vam saw it done.
row    P0A01L00 1900 [44] Will you take the ring that marks you as one
row    P0A01L00 1900 [44] of us, %pcf - or bind yourself to the family
row    P0A01L00 1900 [9] in blood?
label  P0A01L00 1901 [22] Take the ring of %vam.
label  P0A01L00 1902 [29] Swear the blood-oath instead.
row    P0A01L00 1903 [42] Excellent, %pcf. You'll make a fine member
row    P0A01L00 1903 [42] of %vam. Welcome to the family. I am known
row    P0A01L00 1903 [44] as _questgiver_. %vam will continue to watch
row    P0A01L00 1903 [42] your progress, and we may contact you from
row    P0A01L00 1903 [42] time to time on family business. Your oath
row    P0A01L00 1903 [34] is sworn, and the blood remembers.
row    P0B10L08 1900 [43] So the Prince's coven has felt the teeth of
row    P0B10L08 1900 [37] %vam. Tell me, %pcf - is the Coven of
